    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I changed to store and compare telephones in E.164 form.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**`util/TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 replaced the \"strip to bare digits\" logic with E.164 normalization:\n- Keeps a leading `+` and country code when present.\n- Otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits.\n- Strips spaces, dashes and brackets (any non-digit).\n- Requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, throwing `InvalidTelephoneException` otherwise.\n- Idempotent: an already-E.164 value re-normalizes to itself, so duplicate comparison stays correct.\n\n**`rest/advice/InvalidTelephoneException.java`** (new) + **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mapped to **400 Bad Request**, so an unformattable number is rejected (the general handler would otherwise have returned 500).\n\n**`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 the entity's stored-form validation changed from `^[0-9]{10}$` (and `@Digits`) to `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` so the E.164 value persists.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 loosened the request DTO pattern from exactly-10-digits (`^\\D*(\\d\\D*){10}$`) to `^\\+?[0-9 ()\\-]+$` so `+`, brackets etc. are accepted and the normalizer does the real E.164 check; updated the description/example. (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.)\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the create path already normalized; I refreshed the stale comments and also normalized the telephone in `updateOwner` so the stored form stays consistent. Duplicate detection already ran through `normalize`, so it now compares E.164 values.\n\n## Verification\n- `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678` \u2713\n- `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456` \u2713\n- `12` \u2192 400 \u2713\n\nFull suite: **Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
